id: pm-22rzjp
title: Restore strict unknown-key parity for docs linked-artifact additions
description: "GH-1000 reproduces a regression against closed pm-0v9k: files --add rejects an unrecognized left-hand key while docs --add accepts the same malformed key=value shape as a literal path. Restore the shared SDK parser boundary without removing intentional bare values, and prove parity across CLI and SDK transports."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,linked-artifacts,parsing,regression
created_at: "2026-08-13T22:04:05.768Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T04:00:01.313Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T04:00:00.650Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T04:00:00.650Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: docs --add rejects unknown key=value forms with the same allowed-key refusal as files --add; bare paths and URLs containing no assignment syntax remain accepted; malformed URL-plus-note input cannot mutate tracker state; files/docs CLI and SDK parser parity is tested in a temporary tracker; GH-1000 is linked in evidence
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Files and docs reject unknown assignment keys identically while accepting bare paths and URLs without assignment syntax.
actual_result: The shared SDK parser now routes all assignment-bearing input through strict key validation and rejects malformed input before mutation.
