comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T22:04:05.768Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: pm-0v9k is terminal and claims this parity shipped; the live GH-1000 reproduction is a regression incident, so this item preserves lineage rather than reopening or duplicating the original feature."
  "2026-08-14T23:25:33.551Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-15: active in the coupled workspace-integrity tranche spanning provenance repair, self-indexing health severity, extension-host version coherence, cross-version history repair, and strict linked-artifact parsing. Only these five canonical regression items are claimed; all other tracker work remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-15T01:56:43.198Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-15: linked-artifact additions now route every assignment-bearing value through the structured parser, reject unknown keys consistently across file and docs transports, and preserve bare URL/path compatibility. Focused linked test passed 3/3; complete release verification passed static quality, token surfaces, secrets, 7,334 tests, and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Manual packed acceptance also proved malformed URL-like assignment input fails without partial mutation."
  "2026-08-15T02:58:01.201Z","harness:codex","PR #1016 review evidence 2026-08-15: strict unknown-key routing now distinguishes unmistakable whitespace-free filesystem paths and URLs containing '=' from leading assignment syntax. Windows paths and URL query strings remain valid; malformed URL-plus-note and unknown-key values still fail atomically. Focused tests, typecheck, packed smoke, and exact 7,337-test 100/100/100/100 coverage pass."
  "2026-08-15T03:01:33.015Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: linked parser contract passed 3/3 tests; whitespace-free Windows paths and URLs containing equals signs remain positional while unknown structured assignments fail closed."
  "2026-08-15T03:38:26.623Z","harness:codex","Review follow-up 2026-08-15: CodeRabbit found that URL recognition was not anchored and could classify owner=https://... as a positional URL. Reopened the canonical parser item; the fix will preserve genuine scheme-prefixed URLs while restoring unknown-key rejection."
  "2026-08-15T03:59:02.939Z","harness:codex","Review fix evidence: genuine scheme-prefixed URLs with query equals remain positional, while owner=https://... now routes through the SDK allowlist and fails with usage error. Contract docs now describe the same classification boundary."
  "2026-08-15T04:00:00.043Z","harness:codex","Final exact-head evidence: linked parser contract passed 3/3; repository static assurance passed; full suite passed 7,337/7,337 with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage."
